<Vertical id="CarouselDemo" title="Carousel">
  <Markdown id="ctt" title="Classical Test Theory">
### Classical Test Theory (CTT)

Evaluates tests by number correct (true score) and random measurement error.
  </Markdown>
  <Markdown id="irt" title="Item Response Theory">
### Item Response Theory (IRT)

Models the probability of a correct response as a function of student ability and item parameters, to estimate ability levels.
  </Markdown>
  <Markdown id="rasch" title="Rasch Measurement">
### Rasch Measurement Theory

Like IRT with only one parameter, requiring special items which fit the model, but giving more meaningful measurement units.
  </Markdown>
  <Carousel id="carousel_demo" wrap="true">ctt, irt, rasch</Carousel>
</Vertical>
